ason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled back `payments-worker` to v3.3.0 and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call. The error rate has dropped from 0.18 to 0.002 and the service reports healthy in all three regions.\n\n- **Initial target was wrong:** I first went after `payments-api` (v5.1.0, degraded, 0.18 error rate; rollback target v5.0.0). A human reviewer denied both the rollback and the incident, saying the problem is in `payments-worker`.\n- **Checked `payments-worker`:** v3.4.0 was unhealthy at a 0.18 error rate, and v3.3.0 was its most recent healthy production release. I rolled back to v3.3.0 and opened the incident against `payments-worker`.\n- **`payments-api` is untouched:** it is still on v5.1.0 and still reports unhealthy at a 0.18 error rate. If it is also part of the payments errors, it needs a separate decision, since the reviewer denied the rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}